      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ollama): resolve web search secret refs",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nOllama web search ignored configured `models.providers.ollama.apiKey` SecretRefs at runtime. A SecretRef-shaped apiKey was treated as absent, which allowed ambient `OLLAMA_API_KEY` fallback to authenticate web search with a different credential than the one explicitly configured.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nThe runtime now distinguishes three credential states: available, missing, and blocked. Env-backed SecretRefs are resolved locally for web search, while unavailable or non-env SecretRefs fail closed before any request instead of falling through to ambient env auth.\n\n## User Impact\nUsers who configure an env SecretRef for the Ollama provider key get the expected credential on Ollama web search requests. Misconfigured or non-env SecretRefs now fail with a stable diagnostic instead of making unauthenticated requests or silently using another account's ambient key.\n\n## Evidence\n- `extensions/ollama/src/web-search-provider.ts` resolves configured env SecretRefs and blocks ambient fallback when a configured SecretRef is unavailable.\n- `extensions/ollama/src/web-search-provider.test.ts` covers env SecretRef resolution, missing env SecretRefs with ambient env present, and non-env SecretRefs with ambient env present.\n\n## Proof\n- `OPENCLAW_VITEST_FS_MODULE_CACHE_PATH=.vitest-cache-ollama-secretref node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/ollama/src/web-search-provider.test.ts` (18 tests passed)\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check extensions/ollama/src/web-search-provider.ts extensions/ollama/src/web-search-provider.test.ts`\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxlint extensions/ollama/src/web-search-provider.ts extensions/ollama/src/web-search-provider.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode commit --commit HEAD --engine claude` (clean)\n",
        "branch": "llagy007/ollama-web-search-secretref-20260712",
